# Line-ending policy.
#
# Keep shell-executed files LF on every platform. Git for Windows defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true, which would otherwise rewrite these to CRLF on checkout
# and break them under Git Bash / WSL:
#   - `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`  -> "bad interpreter: No such file or directory"
#   - GNU make recipes with a trailing \r  -> "command not found" on the CR
#
# Without this file the Makefile and agent_app/scripts/*.sh silently break for
# Windows users even though `make doctor` reports a healthy environment.
Makefile     text eol=lf
*.sh         text eol=lf
*.bash       text eol=lf
*.yml        text eol=lf
*.yaml       text eol=lf
